# 5. AI agents are a strategic priority right now

Their Alien partnership is extremely fresh.

OpenAIRE explicitly says the next problem after openness is helping researchers and agents make sense of the volume of information. Their MCP gives agents authoritative metadata, PIDs and structured relations instead of making them work from random web search. ([OpenAIRE][8])

And their stated next direction includes:

> advanced Python tooling for qualitative and quantitative analysis at scale.

([OpenAIRE Innovation][9])

This changes how I would pitch your user.

Don't make the headline:

> “A researcher tracks a query.”

Make it:

> **“What happens to an AI research agent's memory when its authoritative knowledge source changes?”**

Imagine Alien:

```text
AGENT
 │
 ├─ OpenAIRE query Q1
 ├─ OpenAIRE query Q2
 ├─ ScholeXplorer relation R
 │
 ▼
produces:
 Claim A
 Claim B
 Analysis C
```

Three months later:

```text
OpenAIRE changes
```

What happens?

Currently the agent's stored answer may simply persist.

Pāṭala:

```text
